# Symptom: Agilent SureSelect capture kit BED with "browser position" and
#   "track name=..." header lines, followed by data lines where the strand
#   column contains "-" but other lines use "." for unstranded capture regions.
#   Some data lines also have a rich name field containing pipe-delimited
#   transcript IDs (ens|..., ref|...).  SpeedSeq variant calling fails with
#   "Please specify a BAM file or files" because it tries to parse the track
#   header as a region and the `int(region[1])` call fails on "name=...".
